// An empty `Map()` or `Set()` handed through a generic identity: its hole key or element closes
// where the call binds the parameter, and the call's result reads at that closed container.
//
// A literal nothing types is built at the open map's own defaults (a `string` key or set element,
// an `i32` value), so the parameter closes to the same container and the result reads as one.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/README.md, "Template format".
// @@PRELUDE@@
function take<B>(b: B): B { return b }
// @@VALUE@@
take(Map())
// @@TYPE@@
{[string]: i32}
// @@PROOF@@
print(v.length)
// @@WANT@@
0
// @@VALUE2@@
take(Set())
// @@TYPE2@@
Set<string>
// @@PROOF2@@
print(v.length)
// @@WANT2@@
0
